			I added a new static function declaration for buos_monitor. Its purpose is to launch a simple kernel-level shell that handles user commands when no arguments are passed at boot.

---- ALGORITHMS ----
>> C2: Explain how you read and write to the console for the kernel monitor.
			For input, I used input_getc() from Pintos's devices/input.c, which retrieves one character at a time from the keyboard. Each character is echoed back to the console using putchar() so the user can see what they type. Input is stored in a buffer until a newline or carriage return is pressed, then it is parsed as a command. For output, I used printf() to display responses and prompts (BUOS>).

>> C3: Any additional enhancement you implement?
			I implemented three commands:

				- whoami prints my name.

				- exit leaves the monitor and allows the kernel to finish shutting down.

				- Any other input prints "invalid command."
